<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.72 million bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.72 million bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-run Cotton Export Corporation of Pakistan (CEC) said on Saturday 1996/97 (July-June) cotton output had reached a provisional 8.72 million 375-lb bales, down from 9.92 million in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Delivery and ginning figures in million bales (year-ago):</p>
<p>		    Punjab	   Sindh	    Total</p>
<p> Delivery	 6.637 (8.162)  2.084 (1.763)  8.721 (9.925)</p>
<p> Pressed	  6.608 (8.115)  2.081 (1.748)  8.690 (9.904)</p>
<p> Mill sales     5.669 (6.736)  1.862 (1.255)  7.532 (7.991)</p>
<p> Export sales   0.007 (1.022)  0.0006(0.436)  0.0013(1.458)</p>
<p> CEC		nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)</p>
<p> Unsold	   0.96  (0.0003)  0.215 (0.021)  1.175 (0.474)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
